SLLM patch 9 (D042, phase2-decodeprof): argmax over long rows with 1,024 threads per row (greedy sampling of many
rows: ggml's kernel gets 64 threads per row at 32 rows). New files ggml-metal-argmax.{h,m} (dispatch, self-test,
status); the kernel appended to kernels/qmm.metal; hooks in CMakeLists.txt, ggml-metal-device.m (init) and
ggml-metal-ops.cpp (the ARGMAX branch). Off with SLLM_ARGMAX=0.
Against llama.cpp b11669 (source tarball 620d222) after patches 0001-0008, applied with patch -p1 in ggml/.

